<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Taifa of Lérida</h1><p class="st-meta">1039 CE – 1110 CE (approx.) · capital Lleida</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Hudid taifa at Lleida on the Segre, a frontier state facing the Catalan counties that at times rivalled its parent state, Zaragoza.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Lleida</a> belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-march">Upper March</a> governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>. Its governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulayman-ibn-hud">Sulayman ibn Hud</a> ruled Lleida for years before he took Zaragoza in 1039 and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-hud">Hudid dynasty</a>; on his death in 1046 his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-al-muzaffar">Yusuf al-Muzaffar</a> ruled it as an independent kingdom, fighting his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-al-muqtadir">al-Muqtadir</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/taifa-of-zaragoza">Taifa of Zaragoza</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> controlled the fertile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segre">Segre</a> valley and bordered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-barcelona">County of Barcelona</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-urgell">County of Urgell</a>, to whom it paid tribute. Under al-Mundhir (1081-1090) it was joined with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tortosa">Tortosa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denia">Dénia</a>, and he allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> against his brother al-Mutaman of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>, whose commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-cid">El Cid</a> defeated them at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-almenar-1082">Almenar</a> in 1082.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Lleida</a> passed under Almoravid control around 1110. In 1149 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-iv-count-of-barcelona">Ramon Berenguer IV of Barcelona</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ermengol-vi-of-urgell">Ermengol VI of Urgell</a> captured the city, adding it to what became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Principality of Catalonia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/taifa-of-lerida.jpg" alt="Taifa of Lérida" width="320" height="376"><figcaption>Image: Taifa de Zaragoza 1080.png: Tyk (talk · contribs) Reinos de Taifas en 1080.svg: Tyk (talk · contribs) derivative work... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taifa_de_Zaragoza_1080.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1039 CE – 1110 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lleida</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yusuf al-Muzaffar, al-Mundhir Imad al-Dawla, Sulayman Sayyid al-Dawla</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic, Mozarabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Spain</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Taifa of Lleida</dd></dl></aside></div>
